Unit and total lot costs use the recorded basis when balancing sale gains.

========== API ==========

aggregate({ accounts: ['^Income:Capital Gains$'] })

========== FILE ==========

commodity SEK
  default
  format 1,000.00 SEK
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
account Income:Capital Gains
2024-01-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  30 FUND {100 SEK}
  Assets:Cash  -3000 SEK
2024-01-02 Unit lot sale
  Assets:Fund  -10 FUND {100 SEK} @ 120 SEK
  Assets:Cash  1200 SEK
  Income:Capital Gains  -200 SEK
2024-01-03 Total lot sale
  Assets:Fund  -10 FUND {{1000 SEK}} @@ 1200 SEK
  Assets:Cash  1200 SEK
  Income:Capital Gains  -200 SEK
2024-01-04 Missing gain
  Assets:Fund  -10 FUND {100 SEK} @ 120 SEK
  Assets:Cash  1200 SEK

========== OUTPUT ==========

[
  {
    "account": "Income:Capital Gains",
    "commodity": "SEK",
    "quantity": "-400"
  }
]

========== WARNINGS ==========

[UNBALANCED_TRANSACTION] Transaction does not balance: 200 SEK
  {{JOURNAL_PATH}}:20:1

[RESULT_MISMATCH] Realized plus unrealized result differs from cash flows and remaining market value by -200 SEK
  {{JOURNAL_PATH}}:20:1
